  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Breezy conditions and above normal temperatures\ncontinue through this evening.\n\nAs a slow moving upper level low moves across the Great Lakes \nthis afternoon, the pressure gradient will continue to tighten \nbehind a weak surface cold front. This combined with a 30 to 40\nknot low-level jet will support gusty winds across the region \ntoday. The strongest winds will focus northeast of Lake Erie, \nwhere gusts of 30 to 35 mph are expected. A slightly cooler\nairmass will filter in behind the front, but will do little to\nreduce temperatures across WNY, with low to mid 60s persisting.\nFarther east, the airmass has not changed much yet, and with\nsome breaks of sun, temperatures will rise into the lower 70s\nacross the Finger Lakes and into mid CNY.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Unsettled weather and cooler temperatures Friday \nthrough the weekend.\n\nUpper level trough and closed low will move across the eastern \nGreat Lakes region Friday through Saturday, where an additional \ncold front is progged to move across the region, supporting \ntemperatures to trend cooler for the end of the week and into \nthe weekend. The cooler weather combined with modest moisture \nwill support daytime shower activity. Additionally, cool wrap \naround moisture on the backside of the surface low Friday night \nthrough Saturday night will support lake enhanced showers \neast/southeast of the lakes. Confidence in rain shower coverage\ndecreases Sunday and into the early next week as models diverge\nin the evolution of the mid-level trough.",
